#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Render the exact fourteen-qubit fourth-order construction offline."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def tex(value,display=False):
    tag='div' if display else 'span'
    return '<'+tag+' class="math" data-tex="'+html.escape(value,quote=True)+'"'+(' data-display="true"' if display else '')+'></'+tag+'>'
def main():
    state=json.loads((HERE/'basis.json').read_text())
    assert json.loads((HERE/'verification.json').read_text())['passed']
    assert json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text())['passed']
    css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-spin2-inertia/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)
    body='''<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent subspaces · Exact radical state</p><a class="back-link" href="../../index.html#n=14&amp;t=4&amp;subspace=radical-n14-k1-t4">← Return to the catalogue</a><h1>Fourteen qubits at fourth order</h1><p class="lead">An analytical reconstruction of the five-component numerical state in ACLiege.jl. All four-qubit reduced-state entries are verified exactly.</p><div class="result"><strong>Proved maximum dimension</strong>'''+tex(r'\boxed{K(14,4)=1}',True)+'''<p>The state below attains the dimension bound. Its AC order is exactly four.</p></div><h2>Five nonzero Dicke coefficients</h2><p>Use normalized Dicke states, with the superscript denoting the number of excitations.</p>'''+tex(state['basis'][0]['stateLatex'],True)+tex(state['basis'][0]['coefficientDefinitionLatex'],True)+'''<p>All other coefficients vanish. Complex conjugation and every collective rotation give further exact fourth-order AC states. Their one-dimensional spans are AC subspaces; arbitrary linear combinations of different representatives are not asserted to be AC.</p><p><a href="../../index.html#n=14&amp;t=4&amp;subspace=radical-n14-k1-t4">Inspect the exact coefficients and Majorana sphere ↗</a> · <a href="basis.json">Download the analytical coefficients ↓</a></p><h2>How the coefficients are determined</h2><p>The five occupied Dicke indices correspond to spin labels '''+tex(r'm=6,3,0,-3,-6')+'''. Matching the first four diagonal spin moments fixes the probabilities uniquely:</p>'''+tex(r'(|c_1|^2,|c_4|^2,|c_7|^2,|c_{10}|^2,|c_{13}|^2)=\frac1{3645}(854,364,1209,364,854).',True)+'''<p>The support spacing eliminates shifts one, two and four. The remaining third-step coherence conditions determine the phases. In the pairwise-equal convention, a useful exact phase invariant is</p>'''+tex(r'\frac{A^2}{|A|^2}=\frac{-265+27i\sqrt{39431}}{5368}.',True)+'''<p>The complete reduction check includes the remaining off-diagonal conditions, rather than only the diagonal moments.</p><h2>Exact verification</h2><p>Split the Dicke coefficients between four and ten qubits:</p>'''+tex(r'M_{ab}=c_{a+b}\sqrt{\frac{\binom4a\binom{10}b}{\binom{14}{a+b}}},\qquad 0\le a\le4,\quad0\le b\le10.',True)+tex(r'MM^\dagger=\frac{I_5}{5},\qquad 2|A|^2+2|B|^2+|C|^2=1.',True)+'''<p>Two separate verifiers reconstruct all 25 entries using exact arithmetic. The independent verifier also checks the alternative phase convention and the source numerical state.</p><h2>Exactly fourth order</h2>'''+tex(r'\operatorname{Tr}(\rho_5^2)=\frac{15209}{90750}=\frac16+\frac{42}{45375}>\frac16.',True)+'''<p>Thus this representative is not fifth-order AC. A separate <a href="../n14-t5/index.html">exact three-copy positivity certificate</a> now excludes every fifth-order state at fourteen qubits, so four is the globally maximum pure-state AC order.</p><h2>Why the subspace dimension is optimal</h2><p>For a fourth-order AC subspace, tensor operators of ranks zero, one and two produce nine mutually orthogonal images of every basis vector. They must fit in the fifteen-dimensional symmetric spin space:</p>'''+tex(r'9k\le15\quad\Longrightarrow\quad k\le1.',True)+'''<p>The exact state supplies the matching lower bound. No symmetry assumption is needed for this upper bound.</p><h2>Two rotation-inequivalent branches</h2><p>The state and its complex conjugate both have proper rotational symmetry group '''+tex(r'D_3')+'''. The nonzero rank-five component rules out any larger polyhedral group, and the nonzero Dicke support fixes the maximal axial rotation order at three. Thus the threefold axis is unique.</p><p>Every rotation relating the two branches would preserve that axis up to sign. Such rotations preserve '''+tex(r'R=c_1c_{13}/(c_4c_{10})')+''', while complex conjugation replaces its nonreal phase by its conjugate. Therefore the branches cannot be related by a collective rotation. This gives two exact rotation families, without claiming that they exhaust every fourth-order state at this size.</p><h2>Source and reproducibility</h2><p>The numerical source is John Martin’s fourteen-qubit representative in <a href="../../references/ACLiege.jl">ACLiege.jl, line 138</a>. A global phase and collective rotation about the third axis put its coefficients in the pairwise-equal convention used here. Decimal agreement identifies the reconstruction; the symbolic reduced-matrix identities establish exact existence independently.</p><p><a href="proof.tex">Complete LaTeX derivation ↓</a> · <a href="verify.py">Exact verifier ↓</a> · <a href="verification.json">Verification report ↓</a> · <a href="verify_independently.py">Independent verifier ↓</a> · <a href="independent-verification.json">Independent report ↓</a></p><footer><a href="../general-bounds/index.html">General AC-subspace bounds ↗</a></footer>'''
    head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Fourteen qubits: an analytical fourth-order AC state</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
    (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+body+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
